  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Licoricone and HEp-2 through a series of target interactions. Licoricone is implicated in targeting Aconitate hydratase, mitochondrial, which is a target of (2S)-3-(4-hydroxy-3,5-dimethoxyphenyl)propane-1,2-diol and Macluraxanthone B. Both of these compounds are predicted to have a target on HEp-2, indicating a possible pathway through which Licoricone may influence the cell line. Similarly, Licoricone is also linked to Protein kinase C eta, which is targeted by a complex molecule that also affects HEp-2. These findings suggest that Licoricone may exert its effects on HEp-2 via multiple molecular mechanisms, possibly through the modulation of enzymes and signaling pathways. The evidence is consistent with a role for Licoricone in influencing HEp-2, but the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
